Verse 1:
[C7]The [F]Lord’s [C7]my [F]Shep[Gm]herd, [F]I’ll [C]not [F]want.
He [G]makes me down [G7]to [C]lie
[F]In pastures [C]green; [F]He [Gm]lea[C]d[C7]eth [F]me
The [Gm]quiet [F]wa[C]ters [F]by.

Verse 2:
[C7][F]My [C7]soul [F]He [Gm][F]doth [C]restore [F]again.
[G]And me [G7]to walk [C]doth make
[F][C]Within [F]the [Gm][C]paths [C7]of [F]righteousness,
[Gm]E'en [F]for His [C]own [F]name's sake.

Verse 3:
[C7]Yea, [F]though [C7]I [F]walk [Gm]in [F]death's [C]dark [F]vale,
[G]Yet will [G7]I fear [C]no ill,
[F]For [C]Thou [F]art [Gm]with [C]me; [C7]and [F]Thy rod
[Gm]And [F]staff [C]me [F]comfort still.

Verse 4:
[C7][F]My [C7][F]table [Gm]Thou [F][C]hast [F]furnished
[G]In [G7]presence of [C]my foes;
[F]My [C]head [F]Thou [Gm]dost [C]with [C7]oil [F]anoint,
[Gm]And [F]my [C]cup [F]overflows.

Verse 5:
[C7][F]Goodness [C7]and [F]mercy [Gm][F]all [C]my [F]life
[G]Shall [G7]surely [C]follow me;
[F][C]And [F]in [Gm][C]God's [C7]house [F]forevermore
[Gm]My [F]dwelling [C]place [F]shall be.
